WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:06.150
Mr. T. rose to fame in 1982 with his appearance
in Rocky III as Rocky's nemesis Clubber Lang,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.150
then truly became a star the following year
with his role as B.A.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.780
Baracus in the hit TV series The A-Team.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.430
Less commonly known by his real name, Laurence
Tureaud, Mr. T was ever-present on TV screens

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.090
for more than a decade of domination.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.260
His star's fallen to some extent over the
years, leaving audiences worldwide wondering:

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.170
does he still pity fools?

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.970
Here's the truth about what happened to Mr.
T.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.210
Still a pitchman

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.440
Outside of his acting roles, Mr. T may be
best known as an advertising pitch man.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.649
Whether he's hawking Snickers bars, his own
cereal, or World of Warcraft, his ads have

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:39.790
always been able to get your attention, if
nothing else.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:45.570
“Now you can have the greatest hair in the
World of Warcraft with the mohawk grenade.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.760
Yeah, wherever I go I’m making Warcraft
look gooood!”

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.600
Recently he's appeared in ads for Fuze Iced
Tea, in which he makes it clear that the years

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.719
have done nothing to affect his charisma.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:58.120
Seriously, he might be ageless.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.360
You can judge for yourself, but he looks exactly
the same.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:06.190
“The only thing bolder than Fuze Iced Tea
is me!”

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.240
Wrestling Hall of Fame

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.010
Mr. T may have entered the popular consciousness
as a fictional boxer in 1982's Rocky III,

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.970
but by 1985, the actor behind Clubber Lang
had made the leap to real wrestling, serving

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:23.140
as tag-team partner to Hulk Hogan versus "Rowdy"
Roddy Piper and Mr. Wonderful at the inaugural

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.140
WrestleMania.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.330
This gave rise to a feud which lasted years
between Mr. T and Piper, who already had little

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:29.590
respect for the actor-turned-wrestler.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.020
“There was no love in that ring.”

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.990
Some felt he'd never paid his dues as a performer
in the ring, but when Mr. T was finally inducted

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.670
into the WWE's Hall of Fame in 2014, he and
Piper finally made peace the old fashioned

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.729
way: on Twitter.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:43.729
Battling cancer

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:49.840
One of the reasons Mr. T decreased his workload
was his 1995 cancer diagnosis for T-cell lymphoma.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.100
He took on the unwelcome opponent the only
way he knew how — aggressively — telling

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.310
Coping with Cancer magazine, quote, "Can you
imagine that?

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.399
Cancer with my name on it.

00:01:58.399 --> 00:01:59.399
Personalized cancer."

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:01.610
“I’ve been through alot in my life.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:03.270
I’ve faced some tough opponents.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:08.590
But now it’s time to face my toughest opponent
of all...me.”

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:13.639
He wrote an as-yet unpublished book on his
experience with author Joyce Brooks, called

00:02:13.639 --> 00:02:17.989
Cancer Saved My Life (Cancer Ain't For No
Wimps), in which he said, quote, "If you don't

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:21.269
remind me that I have cancer then I won't
remember either, because I am too busy living."

00:02:21.269 --> 00:02:22.269
“It’s a blessing.

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:26.829
I’ve been, uh, I’m a cancer survivor for
12 years, you know, so I’ve been through

00:02:26.829 --> 00:02:27.829
a lot, you know.

00:02:27.829 --> 00:02:29.579
It’s uh...been peaks and valleys, you know.

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:32.519
Every day, you don’t feel 100%, but uh...I
made it through.”

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.489
A whole world's worth of fools

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:40.379
In 2011, Mr. T set up shop across the Atlantic
for a show on BBC 3 called World's Craziest

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:41.379
Fools.

00:02:41.379 --> 00:02:43.269
“We got fools with chainsaws.

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:45.269
We got fools breakin’ the law.

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:49.940
We got karate fools with fists flyin’, and
feet jumpin’ all over the place.”

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.019
A compendium of "can-you-believe-this" clips
captured from cameras around the world, the

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:57.989
show ran for 20 episodes before going off
the air in March of 2013.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:02.079
The show, a throwback in the age of YouTube,
also used animated segments to illustrate

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:04.329
the antics of more egregious fools.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:08.029
The series looked like it was going to be
a hit, but it ended after two short seasons.

00:03:08.029 --> 00:03:10.480
“Never celebrate too early.”

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.349
I Pity the Tool

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:16.890
Mr. T surprised both Al Roker and the rest
of America in 2015 when he paid a visit to

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.299
the Today show to make an unexpected announcement:
a new home improvement show called I Pity

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:22.540
the Tool.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:28.199
“I majored in brick masonry.

00:03:28.199 --> 00:03:29.199
I did carpentry.

00:03:29.199 --> 00:03:30.199
So I know what I’m doing.

00:03:30.199 --> 00:03:31.199
I’m good with my hands, whether fighting
or building.”

00:03:31.199 --> 00:03:32.510
The DIY Network aired one episode of I Pity
the Tool and as yet hasn't commented on whether

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.120
or not they'll follow up with more.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.199
The reason why is a mystery, owing to either
viewer turnout or something more behind-the-scenes.

00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:39.709
Is it a pity?

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:40.709
Seems likely.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:44.730
“Don’t be dumb and hit your thumb!”

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.139
Mister Tweet

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:49.999
Mr. T doesn't just pity fools — he turns
that pity into positive action through his

00:03:49.999 --> 00:03:54.379
uplifting Twitter feed, which is full of good
vibes and support informed often by his born-again

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:57.540
Christian faith, along with comments on the
world as he sees it.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.379
He explained his philosophy during a eulogy
for First Lady Nancy Reagan, saying, quote,

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:03.529
"I am not a Republican nor am I a Democrat.

00:04:03.529 --> 00:04:07.010
I am just a Christian Brother from the Hood
trying to do some good!"

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.510
Often heard and not seen

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.999
Starting with his '80s Saturday morning cartoon
series, sensibly titled Mister T, our mohawked

00:04:12.999 --> 00:04:16.880
friend has stayed busy doing voice work for
a variety of projects — from cartoon series

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.880
like Eek!

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.939
The Cat, Sabrina the Animated Series, and
Pecola, through TV movies like the 1987 version

00:04:21.939 --> 00:04:24.490
of Alice Through the Looking Glass, in which
he played the Jabberwocky.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.870
“One little girl?

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.250
Ho ho ho!

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.639
Piece of cake!”

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:31.310
He's even been heard on the big screen in
recent years through his work as the voice

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:36.650
of Earl Devereaux in 2009's hit animated feature
Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.730
“My chest hairs are tingling.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.320
Something’s wrong!”

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.030
And gamers of a certain age have no doubt
recognized his dulcet tones in the Lego Dimensions

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.220
game, in which he appeared as his A-Team character,
B.A.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.220
Baracus.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.220
“That’s B.A.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.220
Baracus.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.220
The B.A. stands for…”

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.220
“...bad attitude!”

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.080
Some heroes are simply timeless.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.080
Thanks for watching!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.449
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:01.729
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

